  "assessment": "The change adds a new sorting module `ledgerout/ordering.py`. I assumed this module is intended to replace or provide the sorting logic used by `run.py`, as no other files were modified to integrate it. The scope of the fix relies entirely on the correctness of `ordering.py`.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Sorting by string representation ('1', '10') leads to lexicographical ordering where '1' precedes '10'.",
      "at": "ledgerout/ordering.py:9 (sort_key function)",
      "call": "python run.py",
      "defect": "The sorting key converts sequence numbers to strings (`str(record['seq'])`), causing lexicographical ordering. This results in the exact failure reported ('sequence 1 is followed by 10'), as '1' sorts before '10' alphabetically.",
      "expected": "Sequence records should be sorted numerically (e.g., ..., 9, 10) to ensure contiguous replayability."
    }
  ]
